    "done_when": "Context: the process-global support clip mode (nova/equilibrium/forward_operator.py _SUPPORT_CLIP_MODE, set_support_clip_mode and support_clip_mode) is being retired. Every benchmark has migrated: the certificate hub, the shared helpers and the leaves now thread an explicit mode through ForwardFluxOperator.with_clip_mode, ForwardSolveRequest(clip_mode=...) and the helpers' clip_mode keyword. This node migrates the seven test modules that still set the global: test_equilibrium_forward_operator, test_exact_clip_memory, test_exact_clip_seed, test_exact_clip_seed_bracket, test_exact_moment_reduction_cut_cells, test_forward_moment_class and test_solve_path_census_inputs. tests/test_forward_support_clip_mode.py, tests/test_forward_solve_clip_mode_request.py and tests/test_forward_solve_clip_mode_bridge.py test the global itself and stay for the deletion node. Rules: every set_support_clip_mode call, and every fixture that sets and restores the global, becomes an explicit mode on the operator or request the test builds, or the clip_mode keyword of the benchmark helper it calls. Each test asserts the same thing it asserted before, under the same mode. Gate, logged under the run directory: (1) grep finds no set_support_clip_mode or support_clip_mode in the seven files; (2) the seven modules, run with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu and -m 'slow or not slow' in one fresh pytest process per file, add no failure by test id against the dispatch base. Run any module over ten minutes through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/nova_lane/run.sh --rungs h200 --force-submit, authorised. Record baseline_suite and after_suite as single JSON objects with literal commands and failure_ids. For the base arm use a git archive of the dispatch base restricted to nova tests benchmarks scripts under /tmp, removed before the manifest is written. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. The manifest's status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
